 "For Story 021.0, this rule also provides targeted auto-fix capabilities: when run with `--fix`, it can (1) insert a safe, non-semantic file-level `@supports` placeholder template at the top of matching test files when the annotation is missing, including clear TODO guidance for humans to replace the template with a real story and requirement reference, and (2) normalize malformed `[REQ-XXX]` prefixes that already contain an identifiable requirement ID, correcting spacing, bracket/parenthesis usage, underscores, and casing while preserving the original ID text and never inventing new requirement identifiers."

- Documents options consistent with the story:
 - `autoFixTestTemplate` – enables file-level `@supports` placeholder insertion (default true).
 - `autoFixTestPrefixFormat` – enables safe normalization of malformed `[REQ-XXX]` prefixes (default true).
 - `testSupportsTemplate` – custom placeholder template string used when inserting file-level `@supports` annotations.

